         (nu = 1 gives Q = 1.000000000)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1d.  THE SIGN.  The candidate's tensor is the SUPERSEDED arm's -- read from the frozen pre-registration
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  READ ONLY, verbatim from prep_2026/gaia_dr4_prep/PREREGISTRATION_DR4.md, Amendment 10(a) and 10(d2):
      "the point-mass response in the external field is ANISOTROPIC, B_par = nu(y_extN) = 1.4732 along the
       external field and B_perp = nu/sqrt(1+L0) = 1.2598 across it (L0 = 0.3674, canonical)"
      "That sign was MI-arm-derived (the MI tensor is perpendicular-dominant everywhere).  The MG solve
       gives a RADIUS-DEPENDENT sign: parallel-dominant at saturation (B_par = 1.4732 > B_perp = 1.2598),
       perpendicular-dominant in the transition zone, with the computed flip at r = 1.96 r_M"

  The candidate is built on gamma_perp^2 = nu(e), gamma_par^2 = d(nu g)/dg -- the MI/algebraic-inertia
  response tensor, which is perpendicular-dominant at EVERY radius (Q > 1 everywhere in its own table).
  The operative arm has been MODIFIED GRAVITY since 2026-08-08.  Its saturation value is
      Q_MG(saturation) = sqrt(B_perp/B_par) = sqrt(1.2598/1.4732) = 0.9247
  i.e. PARALLEL-dominant, Q < 1 -- the OPPOSITE SIDE OF 1 from every entry in the candidate's table.
  [PASS] 1d1 REPORTED AGAINST THE CANDIDATE: the proposed Q is computed in the superseded MODIFIED-INERTIA arm.  In the operative MODIFIED-GRAVITY arm the frozen pre-registration's own solved tensor puts Q on the other side of 1 at saturation.  This check PASSES if the two arms genuinely disagree in SIGN, i.e. if the candidate's headline number is arm-contingent
         (candidate (MI arm) Q_asym = 1.1412 > 1; frozen MG-arm saturation Q = 0.9247 < 1.  A quantity whose SIGN depends on which arm of the theory is operative is not a Kepler-grade law of the theory)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  DILUTION D1 -- THE INTERNAL FIELD.  Q(s) from the exact nonlinear two-body solve at real separations
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The eigenvalue ratio in part 1 is the limit h << g_ext, h = G M/(2 s^2).  Real wide binaries do not
  sit in that limit.  Solve a_rel exactly at each separation and read the radial response.
  El-Badry EDR3, h15 clean cut reproduced: N = 39702 pairs, median M_tot = 1.099 Msun, median s = 0.72 kAU

