----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.  DILUTIONS D2 + D3 -- THE ORBIT AND THE PROJECTION.  End-to-end forward Monte Carlo
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Framework and Newton are run on the SAME orbital draws.  Observable: vtilde = v_proj/sqrt(GM/s_proj).
  Q_obs is the DOUBLE ratio  [med vtilde_perp(F)/med vtilde_perp(N)] / [med vtilde_par(F)/med vtilde_par(N)],
  i.e. exactly gamma_perp/gamma_par as a survey forms it.  Lines of sight drawn from the REAL (l,b) of the
  clean El-Badry sample, so the sky coverage is the data's own and not an assumption.
  <cos^2(LOS, g_ext)> over the real sky distribution = 0.3394 (isotropic would be 0.3333); the sample is high-latitude, which HELPS: the test has no power when the
  line of sight is along g_ext, and that geometry is under-represented here.
    ran Route A / canonical / primary
    ran Route A / alt       / primary
    ran Route A / canonical / alt gext
    ran alpha=0.4 / canonical / primary
    ran alpha=3   / canonical / primary
    ran sqrt(frozen) / canonical / primary
    ran NEWTON

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
