  inverse-variance combination over separation bins: Q_obs - 1 = -0.00642 +- 0.01394  -> 0.46 sigma on the present EDR3 clean sample
  the same combination for the ROBUST signal -- the instantaneous radial response, which needs no orbit
  model at all and is therefore free of the a-prior sensitivity this repository has already documented
  (real_research/data/widebinaries/wb_mond_orbit_mc.out): Q_inst - 1 = +0.01493 +- 0.01394 -> 1.07 sigma
  pairs needed for a 3 sigma detection of the ROBUST signal: 7.8x the present clean sample (N = 3.11e+05)
  for reference, the whole El-Badry EDR3 catalogue is 1.82e6 pairs before ANY quality cut, and Gaia DR4 is expected to roughly double to triple the clean yield, not multiply it by 8.
  [FAIL] 4a  CAN FAIL: is Q detectable at 3 sigma in a sample the size of Gaia DR4's expected clean wide-binary yield (taken generously as 5x the present EDR3 clean sample)?  This is criterion (3) for the candidate: either it holds across many systems at RAR-class precision, or it is not Kepler-grade
         (needs 7.8x the present clean sample on the robust signal; DR4 is expected to deliver about 2-3x.  On the orbit-averaged signal the significance is 0.46 sigma.)

