    the proposing script's geometry-only number                           = +0.0540
  [PASS] 4b  the end-to-end forecast must land within an order of magnitude of the FROZEN pre-registered MG-arm split.  If it does not, one of the two pipelines is wrong and the discrepancy must be reported.  (The proposing script's +0.0540 is 12x to 42x the frozen band and fails this test outright.)
         (|Q_inst - 1| = 0.01397 against the frozen band [0.0013, 0.0046]; ratio to the band centre = 4.73.  The proposing script's number is 18x the band centre.)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.  THE UPSILON LEVER -- measured by re-running the entire pipeline at M_tot x 1.5
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The proposing script claims d log Q / d log Upsilon = 0 EXACTLY, on the grounds that gamma ~ M^(-1/2) in
  both bins.  That argument is correct for the NORMALISATION and wrong for the REGIME: the mass sets
  h/g_ext = G M/(2 s^2 g_ext), i.e. which side of the transition each pair sits on.  Measured, not argued:
    (instantaneous radial-response weighted Q at M x 1.0, no orbit model: 1.01397)
    M_tot x 1.0:   sample-weighted Q_obs = 0.99416   sample-weighted gamma_iso = 1.04893
    (instantaneous radial-response weighted Q at M x 1.5, no orbit model: 1.01288)
    M_tot x 1.5:   sample-weighted Q_obs = 0.99641   sample-weighted gamma_iso = 1.04053
    d log Q_obs   / d log Upsilon = +0.0056
    d log gamma_iso / d log Upsilon = -0.0198   (for contrast: the isotropic boost's own lever)
    in the units the candidate is quoted in: Q_obs - 1 moves from -0.00584 to -0.00359 -- an absolute shift of 0.00225 in Q for a 0.18 dex change
    in the mass calibration, against a signal whose whole size is 0.01397.
  [PASS] 5a  REPORTED AGAINST THE CANDIDATE: the claim d log Q / d log Upsilon = 0 EXACTLY holds only for the asymptotic eigenvalue ratio.  For the quantity a survey can form it must be nonzero, because the mass sets the regime.  This check PASSES if the lever is measurably nonzero -- i.e. if the claim is false
         (measured d log Q_obs/d log Upsilon = +0.0056; the ASYMPTOTIC ratio's lever is 0 exactly, and that part of the claim is confirmed -- it is the observable that carries the lever)
  IN THE CANDIDATE'S FAVOUR, and it matters: the lever is still far milder than any galaxy-scale
  Upsilon lever in this hunt, and wide-binary masses come from a main-sequence relation calibrated on
  eclipsing binaries (0.02-0.04 dex) rather than from stellar population synthesis (0.10-0.25 dex).

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- K4 (Q = gamma_perp/gamma_par)
======================================================================================================================
  1. The asymptotic claim REPRODUCES.  Q_asym = 1.1412 (Route A, canonical, primary g_ext); the whole
     kernel class spans 1.0330-1.1746; Newton gives exactly 1 and the mutation control confirms it
     end-to-end.  The frozen Amendment 2 eigenvalues are reproduced to <5e-4 by an independent implementation.
  2. NOT A RESTATEMENT.  Executed: v^4 = G M_b a0 is isotropic, contains no g_ext, and is satisfied
     identically by every kernel in the class -- it produces no number for Q at all.
  3. THE CANDIDATE DOES NOT SURVIVE THE DILUTIONS.  Q(s) at the sample median separation is 1.0000, not 1.1412,
     because the internal field is not small; the orbit averages what is left; and the end-to-end
     sample-weighted Q_obs = 0.9942, which is -4.1% of the intrinsic anisotropy and -0.11x the
     proposing script's geometry-only 1.054.
  4. IT IS NOT MEASURABLE.  -0.46 sigma on the present clean EDR3 sample; a 3 sigma detection needs 8x that sample.
     This AGREES with the frozen pre-registration's own MG-arm number (+0.0013-0.0046),
     computed independently and before this hunt, and with hunt item 15, which measured the split on the
     same catalogue and found it 63x to 793x underpowered.
  5. THE UPSILON LEVER IS NOT ZERO for the observable: d log Q_obs/d log Upsilon = +0.0056.  It is zero
     only for the asymptotic eigenvalue ratio, which is not a measurable quantity.
  6. THE SIGN IS ARM-CONTINGENT.  The candidate's tensor is the superseded MODIFIED-INERTIA one (perp-dominant
     everywhere).  The operative MODIFIED-GRAVITY arm's own frozen solve gives Q = 0.9247 at saturation --
     PARALLEL-dominant, the other side of 1.  This script's orbit Monte Carlo, run on the MI-flavoured
     algebraic law, independently returns Q = 0.9141 in the widest bin, within 0.0106 of that frozen
     MG saturation value -- and the frozen pre-registration already registers the flip at r = 1.96 r_M.
  CATEGORY: the anisotropy is real and Newton-forbidden, but it is NOT Kepler-grade.  Criterion (2) is
  damaged (the coefficient's SIGN depends on which arm is operative) and criterion (3) fails outright on
  measurability.  Recorded as a FAILED candidate.

  WHICH FAILING CHECKS ARE FINDINGS RATHER THAN DEFECTS: 3b2 (the geometry-only 1.054 is not recovered),
  4a (not detectable in DR4) and, where they fail, 4b.  Each is a can-fail check whose failure IS the
  result.  3a1, 3c1, 3c2, 3c3, 1a, 1b, 1c are validation checks and a failure there would void the run.

